He would be unstoppable, just like he was
when he played for the Georgia Bulldogs.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:36.509
And in the NFL, he is also a great person.

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:37.509
Run, Herschelle, run.

00:01:37.509 --> 00:01:38.509
That's a tweet.

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:43.759
In written letter form, he figured out how
to force his way back on to Twitter.

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:46.899
I believe this is a ban evasion, but we'll
talk about that.

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:49.560
And then Donald Trump junior reposts it.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.890
And before you know it, Trump's tweeting,
writing tweet length letters posted by his

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:55.890
family to Twitter.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.980
He then sends a much crazier one.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:03.659
And this is I almost feel bad for the guy.

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:08.000
This is one of the saddest statements I've
ever seen from a President Trump, clearly

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.620
triggered by yesterday's announcement from
Joe Biden that the US has secured an additional

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.120
hundred million doses of the JNJ vaccine.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.120
Donald Trump, quote, tweeting, sort of writing
a letter where he says this is it's almost

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.099
sad, quote, I hope everyone remembers when
they're getting the covid-19 often referred

00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:28.880
to as the China virus vaccine, that if I wasn't
president, you wouldn't be getting that beautiful

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.200
shot for five years at best and probably wouldn't
be getting it at all.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.430
I hope everyone remembers.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.569
Isn't there something really sad about that?

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:38.100
These really are tweets now.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.560
I don't you know, what can Twitter really
do?

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:49.260
Can Twitter ban statements, written statements
